{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Segoe UI;}{\f1 Consolas;}}{\colortbl ;\red49\green139\blue59;}\f0\fs20 \pard\sb140\sa80\b\cf1\fs30 X-Shard \u8212? Component licenses and notices\b0\cf0\fs20\par \pard\sa60 \par \pard\sb140\sa80\b\cf1\fs24 Independent components\b0\cf0\fs20\par \pard\sa60 \par \pard\sa60 \u8226? {\b X-Shard GUI:} GNU GPL version 3; the publisher's supplied declaration and notices follow.\par \pard\sa60 \u8226? {\b extract-xiso:} original modified Berkeley license. Maintained by {\b XboxDev}; originally written by {\b in <in@fishtank.com>}.\par \pard\sa60 \u8226? {\b XGDTool:} GNU GPL version 3, by {\b wiredopposite}. Original repository: https://github.com/wiredopposite/XGDTool.\par \pard\sa60 \u8226? Framework and native-library notices are included in the {\f1 licenses} directory.\par \pard\sa60 \par \pard\sa60 The backends are independent executable programs. Their original licenses govern those components. The X-Shard GUI notices and EULA do not replace, restrict or override rights granted by those third-party licenses. The full GPLv3 text is included below and in {\f1 licenses/GPL-3.0.txt}; the upstream XGDTool source/build archive is included in {\f1 sources}.\par \pard\sa60 \par \pard\sa60 This product includes software developed by in <in@fishtank.com>.\par \pard\sa60 \par \pard\sb140\sa80\b\cf1\fs24 Local application data\b0\cf0\fs20\par \pard\sa60 \par \pard\sa60 X-Shard stores settings, source/destination paths, queue metadata, and the legal-document content hash and acceptance timestamp locally. Processing logs may contain local paths and can be exported locally. These data are not automatically sent to the developer or a third party. XGDTool defaults to offline mode. If you explicitly disable Offline mode for a new job, XGDTool may contact Google (connectivity check), GitHub/Repackinator (title database) and XboxUnity (title IDs and artwork). Some upstream requests use unencrypted HTTP. Title IDs and connection metadata can be disclosed to those services. X-Shard does not contact those services itself; the selected backend performs these optional lookups. The bundled publisher privacy declaration describes the default offline workflow; this section documents the optional online backend feature. External web links open in the system browser only after an explicit click.\par }